  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "In an inverse variation, $y=6$ when $x=-7.$ Find an equation that relates $x$ and $y.$\n\n$\\,y=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Since $y$ varies inversely with $x,$ we use the equation\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{k}{x}.\n$$\n\nNext, we use the given data $y=6$ when $x=-7$ to find $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6 & =\\frac{k}{(-7)} \\\\ 6\\cdot (-7) & =k \\\\ -42 & =k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our inverse variation equation is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{42}{x}.\n$$",
